-- A polymorphic ASSUME has a declared type that holds neither a DEONTIC nor an
-- EVENT: it holds one only where a rule reads it as one, and each read gives it
-- a type of its own. A request has no JSON form for a DEONTIC or an EVENT, so
-- an exported rule that reads the ASSUME as one of them is refused as a written
-- type is, naming the ASSUME. A read as a NUMBER is not refused. The rules are
-- exported on purpose: the same rules without @export check.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Seller, Buyer
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF `deliver goods`, `pay invoice`

GIVEN duty IS A DEONTIC Person Action
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`already fulfilled` duty MEANS
  CONSIDER duty
  WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
  OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN e IS AN EVENT Person Action
GIVETH A NUMBER
`time of` e MEANS
  CONSIDER e
  WHEN EVENT party action time THEN time

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
ASSUME `a placeholder`

-- Refused: the body hands the ASSUME to a helper that takes a DEONTIC.
@export Is the placeholder a fulfilled duty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`placeholder fulfilled` MEANS `already fulfilled` `a placeholder`

-- Refused: the body takes the ASSUME apart as a DEONTIC.
@export Is the placeholder a fulfilled duty, by its own body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`placeholder fulfilled by its body` MEANS
  CONSIDER `a placeholder`
  WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
  OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Refused: the body hands the ASSUME to a helper that takes an EVENT.
@export When did the placeholder happen
GIVETH A NUMBER
`placeholder time` MEANS `time of` `a placeholder`

-- Not exported: reading the ASSUME as a DEONTIC is fine here, and is not reported.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`internal fulfilled` MEANS `already fulfilled` `a placeholder`

-- Accepted: this read gives the ASSUME the type NUMBER, whatever the other rules read it as.
@export One more than the placeholder
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one more` MEANS `a placeholder` + 1
